y issuance tracker, Q3 2026, doc `pellham-offering`).\n- **Another offering was also cut back.** The tracker says two utility share offerings were cut back in size in Q3. The snippet I read names only Pellham's, so I don't know which other utility it was.\n- **Pellham is cutting its plans.** It said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender. A utility that is cutting capex because its raise failed is showing that equity isn't available to it right now.\n- **What the plans cover.** Pellham and Norvane filed 2027 capital plans in October, mostly for substations and transformers. Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria (doc `utility-capex-2027`).\n\n**Limits of this answer:**\n- I did not read the utility tender calendar or Pellham's market statement, so I don't have the plan amounts or the reason the offering was pulled.\n- I did not pull the `utility_spreads` bond-spread series, so I can't say whether debt is a workable alternative. Node n3 is covering debt markets.\n- I found nothing on Norvane's equity plans or on share prices, so I can't say whether Norvane could issue.\n\n**What would change this:** a successful follow-on offering, such as Pellham reopening in Q1 2027, or evidence that the failure was specific to Pellham rather than market-wide.","ttft_ms":3463,"type":"result","duration_ms":29218,"uuid":"99b93586-faac-4abd-a42b-26f0ae0367c3","ttft_stream_ms":3011,"time_to_request_ms":252,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":19,"system_prompt":23,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":20,"input_attachments":37,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":13,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":30,"init_frame_send":12,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":2,"autocompact":13,"request_announcements":29,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":8,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":27,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process